### Real Example
### Plain JavaScript

```bash
<button onclick="changeText()">Click me</button>
<p id="message">Hello</p>

<script>
  function changeText() {
    document.getElementById("message").innerText = "Goodbye";
  }
</script>
```

- Direct DOM access
- Manual state/data tracking
- Imperative


## React

```bash
function App() {
  const [message, setMessage] = React.useState("Hello");

  return (
    <>
      <button onClick={() => setMessage("Goodbye")}>Click me</button>
      <p>{message}</p>
    </>
  );
}
```

- State-driven UI
- Declarative
- Clean separation of logic and  UI
